WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:03.085
Jupiter, which takes twelve of our years.

00:03.785 --> 00:10.820
Jupiter is five times as far from the Sun as we are and needs almost twelve of our years to go round once.

00:11.270 --> 00:16.254
While the Earth goes round one time, Jupiter covers a twelfth of its path.
